<SiteLayout title="File Conversion Guides | ConvertAnyFile" description="Practical guides to image, archive, and structured-data formats, including RAR, 7Z, ZIP, TAR, GZIP, HEIC, WebP, AVIF, JPG, PNG, CSV, and JSON.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Guides</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Conversion guides</span><h1>Understand the format before you convert it.</h1><p>Practical explanations for choosing outputs, avoiding compatibility mistakes, understanding compression and metadata, and deciding when conversion is actually useful.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Why these guides exist</span><h2>Good conversion starts with the destination.</h2><p>A converter can change a container in seconds, but the right output depends on compatibility, structure, metadata, compression, and what the next application expects. These guides explain those trade-offs before you click Convert.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>People-first content</strong><p>Each guide is tied to a real converter or format decision on ConvertAnyFile. The goal is useful format education, not pages created only to repeat keywords.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Current guides</span><h2>Start with the problem you are trying to solve.</h2><p>Image compatibility, archive containers, compression behavior, and structured-data choices are covered because they answer practical conversion decisions.</p></div><div class="category-grid">{guides.map((guide)=><a class="category-card category-card--live" href={guide.href}><div class="category-icon">G</div><div><span class="live-badge">Guide</span><h3>{guide.title}</h3><p>{guide.text}</p></div><span class="category-arrow">→</span></a>)}</div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Archive starting points</span><h2>Common archive questions and the matching tool.</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Your question</th><th>Best starting guide</th><th>Useful tool</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>How do I open a RAR as ZIP?</td><td><a href="/guides/how-to-convert-rar-to-zip/">RAR to ZIP how-to</a></td><td><a href="/rar-to-zip/">RAR to ZIP</a></td></tr><tr><td>How do I make a 7Z easier to share?</td><td><a href="/guides/how-to-convert-7z-to-zip/">7Z to ZIP how-to</a></td><td><a href="/7z-to-zip/">7Z to ZIP</a></td></tr><tr><td>Should I use ZIP or TAR?</td><td><a href="/guides/zip-vs-tar/">ZIP vs TAR</a></td><td><a href="/archive-converter/">Archive Converter</a></td></tr><tr><td>Why is .gz different from .zip?</td><td><a href="/guides/gzip-vs-zip/">GZIP vs ZIP</a></td><td><a href="/gz-to-zip/">GZIP to ZIP</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
